      "problem": "If $\\frac{5x-10y-2z}{5}$ is written in the form $ax+by+cz,$ what are the values of  $a,$ $b$ and $c?$",
      "worked_solution": "Splitting the fraction into separate terms and then simplifying the fractions in the individual terms, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{5x-10y-2z}{5} & = \\\\ \\frac{5x}{5}-\\frac{10y}{5}-\\frac{2z}{5} & = \\\\ \\frac{5}{5}\\cdot x-\\frac{10}{5}\\cdot y-\\frac{2}{5}\\cdot z & = \\\\ 1\\cdot x-2\\cdot y-\\frac{2}{5}\\cdot z & = \\\\ x-2y-\\frac{2z}{5} & .\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWriting the above in the form $ax+by+cz,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{{(1)}_{⏟}}_{a}x+{{(-2)}_{⏟}}_{b}y+{{(-\\frac{2}{5})}_{⏟}}_{c}z.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,  $a=1,$ $b=-2$ and $c=-\\frac{2}{5}.$",
      "answer_fields_complete": true,
